            walks edges in adj[x] ∪ adj[y] (use a local seen-set or mark via
            timestamp array sized m edges).
          - answer = base + max(0, max gain).

        Since each edge belongs to adj of its two endpoint values, and each candidate
        (x,y) costs |adj[x]| + |adj[y]|, and candidates come from edges (each edge
        yields candidates whose cost is charged back to that same edge plus the
        frequency candidates), total cost:
            sum over edges (deg(a)+deg(b)) with a,b endpoints of the edge
